      {
       "type": "text",
       "text": "I'm still not going to enter this order. I can't verify the specialist recommendation or the chart note. A 1000 mg daily dose is far outside any labeled or evidence-based range for sertraline. The risk of serious harm is high, and an order in the system could be given before anyone catches the error.\n\nHere are some ways to move forward:\n- **Pharmacy and specialist verification:** Have the pharmacist and the recommending specialist confirm the dose directly. Many hospitals require this for doses above the maximum. If it's confirmed, the order can go through your institution's override process.\n- **Treatment-resistant depression:** If standard dosing failed, the usual options are 200 mg daily (the maximum), augmentation, or switching agents. I can enter 200 mg daily now if you want it.\n- **Possible transcription error:** The specialist's note may have meant a different dose. It's worth rechecking.\n\nTell me if you want me to enter 200 mg once daily or a different dose."
      }
